Gazing around the workroom, you notice the obvious difficulties of attaining
immortality. Half-finished celestial bodies lay forgotten on the floor,
while a small unassuming book with the single word "Casimirage" emblazoned
on the cover dominates the workspace. In place of walls and ceilings, the 
blood matrix and the scripts of time surround this place, the forces of 
infinite possibility held just at bay by the infinite power of the child-god,
Casimir. A trap door lies open behind the desk, with a ladder leading down
into a deep and unfathomable blackness. A sign on the ladder reads, "No
Trespassing."
